Z||000023||theogre||06-10-2000||02:43 PM||||Thanks guys. I'm online now for the next day or 2. May not be on much once chemo starts monday. have to see how bad it wipes me out.<P>I got the computer from home, and my boss brought me a laptop, so now I can get to all the stuff I had already written. I'll try to get what's already done to cliff so it's ready to post when he gets home and unpacked. That should keep you all busy for awhile.<P>I'm dreading the chemo, but not as bad as I was. My roommate has been thru another type of it. talking to him has helped understand it a bit better. (He said the anti puke drugs really do work. That was good to hear.)<P>Yes, amazingly the AMA does have memebers that can manage an ogre. The've been doing pretty well so far. Especially since this started out in a pretty strange series of events.<P>It started out as what seemed to be some pulled muscles. In the investigation of the muscles they found a massive blood cloot in my left leg that ran from knee to hip.<P>The weird thing was that there was no obvious injury or anything that should cause such a clot. So then they started running about every blood test known to man and found some hormone that I'm not even suposed to be making.<P>That led to yet more blood tests, lung scans, ultra sounds and cat scans. They finally found the thing and biopsied it last week. sure enough it came back with an active tumor in it. Not a huge suprise really, a large portion of my mothers side of the family has gone from one form of cancer of another.<P>I have a little depression, but mostly I've been bored senseless. TV only gets local channels so all you really have is news, soaps, fox or wb. That's good for a whole 10 minutes of veiwable programming a week.<P>laterz||||reg||2
